{"name":"Bunting","hex":"#2b3449","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bunting","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A botanical plant name author abbreviation for botanist R.H. Bunting (fl. 1923)."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname transferred from the nickname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bunting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Emberiza","blocks":[{"text":"The buntings are a group of Old World passerine birds forming the genus Emberiza, the only genus in the family Emberizidae. The family contains 44 species. They are seed-eating birds with stubby, conical bills that inhabit open and half-open habitats, including deserts, stony drylands, shrubland, savanna, and open taiga forests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Goldammer_Emberiza_citrinella.jpg/330px-Goldammer_Emberiza_citrinella.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emberiza","wikidata":"Q614481"},{"title":"Passerina","blocks":[{"text":"The genus Passerina is a group of birds in the cardinal family (Cardinalidae). Although not closely related to the buntings in the family Emberizidae, they are sometimes known as the North American buntings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/PaintedBunting23.jpg/330px-PaintedBunting23.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Passerina","wikidata":"Q609717"},{"title":"Bunting (animal behavior)","blocks":[{"text":"Bunting is a form of animal behavior, often found in felids, in which the animal butts or rubs its head against other things, including people. Bunting is generally considered to be a form of territorial scent-marking behaviour, where the cat rubs the scent glands on its cheeks and forehead on the object being marked."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Real_life_best_friends_%28Unsplash%29.jpg/330px-Real_life_best_friends_%28Unsplash%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunting_(animal_behavior)","wikidata":"Q25203399"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/A_Rare_Crested_Bunting_%2850027361348%29.jpg/500px-A_Rare_Crested_Bunting_%2850027361348%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/A_Rare_Crested_Bunting_%2850027361348%29.jpg/1280px-A_Rare_Crested_Bunting_%2850027361348%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/A_Rare_Crested_Bunting_%2850027361348%29.jpg/500px-A_Rare_Crested_Bunting_%2850027361348%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Rare_Crested_Bunting_(50027361348).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Emberiza_siemsseni.jpg/500px-Emberiza_siemsseni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Emberiza_siemsseni.jpg/1280px-Emberiza_siemsseni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Emberiza_siemsseni.jpg/500px-Emberiza_siemsseni.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmberiza_siemsseni.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Corn_Bunting._Miliaria_calandra_%2832291261152%29.jpg/500px-Corn_Bunting._Miliaria_calandra_%2832291261152%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Cor